cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ALE outcome predictor — GSM-flux + ESM2 sequence-fusion prediction of adaptive-laboratory-evolution gene targets"
abstract: >-
  A predictor that ranks which genes a microbial genome is most likely to
  mutate under a defined adaptive-laboratory-evolution (ALE) selection,
  conditioned on genome-scale metabolic-model (GSM) flux features and ESM2
  protein-sequence embeddings. Trained and evaluated end-to-end on five real
  ALEdb E. coli selections (86 convergent positives) with leakage-free
  cluster-aware cross-validation. Flux features represent real convergence
  in-distribution but are bounded by flux-degeneracy and blind to the
  regulatory and structural majority of targets; fusing flux with ESM2
  sequence embeddings beats flux alone in roughly 73% of CV seeds by
  recovering flux-blind genes. A proof-of-concept on a deliberately small
  curated corpus that drops onto the full ALEdb when pulled locally.
